      {
        "id": "lem-almost-invariant-vectors-and-positive-type-functions",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Almost invariant vectors and normalized positive type functions",
        "deps": [
          "def-almost-invariant-vectors-for-a-unitary-representation",
          "def-matrix-coefficient-of-a-unitary-representation",
          "def-continuous-function-of-positive-type",
          "thm-gns-construction-for-topological-groups",
          "cor-normalized-positive-type-functions-correspond-to-pointed-cyclic-representations",
          "def-hilbert-direct-sum-of-unitary-representations",
          "def-strongly-continuous-unitary-representation",
          "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
          "def-compact-space",
          "def-topological-group",
          "def-hilbert-space",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $G$ be a topological group and let $(\\pi,H)$ be a strongly continuous unitary representation. Then $\\pi$ has almost invariant vectors ([[def-almost-invariant-vectors-for-a-unitary-representation]]) if and only if there is a net $(\\xi_i)_{i\\in I}$ of unit vectors in $H$ such that the normalized positive type functions $\\varphi_i(g)=\\langle\\pi(g)\\xi_i,\\xi_i\\rangle$ ([[def-matrix-coefficient-of-a-unitary-representation]], [[def-continuous-function-of-positive-type]]) converge to the constant function $1$ uniformly on every compact subset of $G$. Consequently, if $(\\varphi_i)_{i\\in I}$ is a net of normalized continuous functions of positive type on $G$ converging to $1$ uniformly on compacta, with GNS triples $(\\pi_{\\varphi_i},\\xi_{\\varphi_i})$ as in [[thm-gns-construction-for-topological-groups]] and [[cor-normalized-positive-type-functions-correspond-to-pointed-cyclic-representations]], then its cyclic vectors are asymptotically invariant: for every compact $Q\\subseteq G$ and every $\\varepsilon>0$ there is $i_0\\in I$ such that $\\xi_{\\varphi_i}$ is $(Q,\\varepsilon)$-invariant for every $i\\ge i_0$, and hence the Hilbert direct sum $\\widehat{\\bigoplus}_{i\\in I}\\pi_{\\varphi_i}$ ([[def-hilbert-direct-sum-of-unitary-representations]]) has almost invariant vectors. Conversely the coefficient net of any net of almost invariant vectors converges to $1$ uniformly on compacta.",
        "strategy": "For a unit vector $\\xi$ and $g\\in G$ the elementary identities $\\lVert\\pi(g)\\xi-\\xi\\rVert^2=2(1-\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\pi(g)\\xi,\\xi\\rangle)$ and $|1-\\langle\\pi(g)\\xi,\\xi\\rangle|\\le\\lVert\\pi(g)\\xi-\\xi\\rVert$ (Cauchy-Schwarz applied to $\\langle\\xi-\\pi(g)\\xi,\\xi\\rangle$, [[thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space]]) show that, on a fixed compact $Q$, the coefficient is close to $1$ exactly when the displacement is small. Given almost invariant vectors, choose for each pair $(Q,\\varepsilon)$ a witness $\\xi_{Q,\\varepsilon}$ and index the net by the directed set of pairs; this is the only choice input, and it is supplied by the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Conversely, the same elementary identity turns uniform convergence of the coefficients to $1$ on a compact set into a small displacement. The final clause is the net form of the same equivalence applied to the GNS triples of the $\\varphi_i$: $\\varphi_i$ is the coefficient of the cyclic vector $\\xi_{\\varphi_i}$ ([[cor-normalized-positive-type-functions-correspond-to-pointed-cyclic-representations]]), so the elementary identity turns the eventual uniform smallness of $|1-\\varphi_i|$ on a compact set into a displacement bound for $\\xi_{\\varphi_i}$, and embedding the witnesses into the Hilbert direct sum exhibits almost invariance of that direct sum. No individual $\\pi_{\\varphi_i}$ is claimed to have almost invariant vectors by itself.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
