        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. For every integer $n\\ge3$ the group $\\mathrm{SL}_n(\\mathbb R)$ (with its Lie group topology as an embedded subgroup of $\\mathrm{GL}_n(\\mathbb R)$, [[ex-general-and-special-linear-lie-groups]]) has Kazhdan's property (T) ([[def-kazhdans-property-t]]).",
        "strategy": "For each ordered triple $(i,j,k)$ with $i\\ne j$ and $k\\notin\\{i,j\\}$ let $G_{ij,k}\\cong\\mathrm{SL}_2(\\mathbb R)\\ltimes\\mathbb R^2$ be the subgroup of $\\mathrm{SL}_n(\\mathbb R)$ consisting of the block matrices acting on $\\mathrm{span}(e_i,e_k)$ with a vector of entries in rows $i,k$ of the remaining column $j$, so that its translation subgroup $N_{ij,k}$ contains $E_{ij}(t)$ for every $t$ and every $(i,j,k)$ ([[def-external-semidirect-product]], [[thm-external-semidirect-product-is-a-group]], [[def-elementary-matrix]]). Let $Q_{ij,k}\\subseteq G_{ij,k}$ be the finite set from [[lem-sl2-r-semidirect-r2-has-relative-property-t]] and let $Q_0=\\bigcup_{(i,j,k)}Q_{ij,k}$, a finite union of compact sets, hence compact. Let $\\delta:=\\min_{(i,j,k)}\\varepsilon_{ij,k}>0$ be the minimum of the constants supplied by that lemma and let $M=M(n)$ be the bound of [[lem-sl-n-r-is-boundedly-generated-by-elementary-root-subgroups]]; put $\\varepsilon:=\\delta/(4M)$. Let $(\\pi,H)$ be a strongly continuous unitary representation with a $(Q_0,\\varepsilon)$-invariant unit vector $\\xi$. For each triple, [[lem-normal-relative-property-t-controls-distance-to-invariant-vectors]] applied to the restriction of $\\pi$ to $G_{ij,k}$ and the relative Kazhdan pair $(Q_{ij,k},\\varepsilon_{ij,k})$, with $\\varepsilon\\le\\varepsilon_{ij,k}$, gives $\\sup_{n\\in N_{ij,k}}\\lVert\\pi(n)\\xi-\\xi\\rVert\\le2\\varepsilon/\\delta\\le1/(2M)$; in particular every elementary transvection $E_{ij}(t)\\in N_{ij,k}$ moves $\\xi$ by at most $1/(2M)$. By the bounded generation lemma every $g\\in\\mathrm{SL}_n(\\mathbb R)$ is a product of at most $M$ transvections, and telescoping the displacement along that product with unitarity gives $\\lVert\\pi(g)\\xi-\\xi\\rVert\\le M\\cdot1/(2M)=1/2$ for every $g$. Hence the closed convex hull $C$ of the orbit $\\pi(\\mathrm{SL}_n(\\mathbb R))\\xi$ is contained in the closed ball of radius $1/2$ about $\\xi$ ([[def-relative-normed-convexity-and-separation]]). $C$ is nonempty, closed and convex, and the nearest-point theorem ([[thm-projection-onto-a-nonempty-closed-convex-set]], which assumes Countable Choice, supplied by AC via [[thm-choice-implies-dependent-implies-countable-choice]], [[def-countable-choice]]) gives a unique point $\\eta\\in C$ of minimal norm; $\\lVert\\eta-\\xi\\rVert\\le1/2$ gives $\\eta\\ne0$, and $C$ is $G$-invariant, so uniqueness of the minimal point and unitarity force $\\pi(g)\\eta=\\eta$ for every $g$. Therefore $(Q_0,\\varepsilon)$ is a compact Kazhdan pair, and [[thm-property-t-is-equivalent-to-the-existence-of-a-kazhdan-pair]] gives property (T). This is the local relative-(T) plus real Gaussian-elimination route of the group-track design; it uses no integer bounded-generation theorem and no higher-rank Lie theory. AC is used for the countable-choice nearest-point theorem and the Hilbert-space suppliers ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]).",
